  "title": { "en": "Weather and seasons", "uz": "Ob-havo va fasllar", "ru": "Погода и времена года", "tr": "Hava durumu ve mevsimler" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Talk about the weather, the seasons and what to wear.",
    "uz": "Ob-havo, fasllar va nima kiyish haqida gapiring.",
    "ru": "Говорите о погоде, временах года и о том, что надеть.",
    "tr": "Hava durumu, mevsimler ve ne giyeceğin hakkında konuş."
  },
  "guide": "rocky",
  "color": "#0EA5E9",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "It is cold, it is raining", "uz": "It is cold, it is raining", "ru": "It is cold, it is raining", "tr": "It is cold, it is raining" },
    "body": {
      "en": "An English sentence always needs a subject, so weather sentences start with \"It is\": It is cold. It is sunny. It is raining. Here \"it\" means nothing, so do not translate it. Question: Is it cold? Negative: It is not cold. Use \"in\" with seasons: in winter. \"What is the weather like?\" means \"How is the weather?\"; here \"like\" is not the verb \"to like\".",
      "uz": "Ingliz tilida gap egasiz bo'lmaydi, shuning uchun ob-havo haqidagi gap \"It is\" bilan boshlanadi: It is cold (Sovuq). It is raining (Yomg'ir yog'yapti). Bu yerda \"it\" hech narsani bildirmaydi va tarjima qilinmaydi. Savol: Is it cold? Inkor: It is not cold. Fasllar \"in\" bilan keladi: in winter (qishda). \"What is the weather like?\" degani \"Ob-havo qanday?\"; bu yerda \"like\" \"yoqtirmoq\" emas.",
      "ru": "В английском предложении всегда нужно подлежащее, поэтому о погоде говорят с \"It is\": It is cold — Холодно. It is raining — Идёт дождь. Слово \"it\" здесь ничего не значит и не переводится. Вопрос: Is it cold? Отрицание: It is not cold. С временами года используется \"in\": in winter — зимой. \"What is the weather like?\" значит \"Какая погода?\"; здесь \"like\" — не глагол \"нравиться\".",
      "tr": "İngilizcede cümle öznesiz olmaz, bu yüzden hava hakkındaki cümleler \"It is\" ile başlar: It is cold (Hava soğuk). It is raining (Yağmur yağıyor). Buradaki \"it\" bir anlam taşımaz ve çevrilmez. Soru: Is it cold? Olumsuz: It is not cold. Mevsimlerle \"in\" kullanılır: in winter (kışın). \"What is the weather like?\" \"Hava nasıl?\" demektir; buradaki \"like\" \"sevmek\" değildir."
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "It is cold today.", "native": { "uz": "Bugun havo sovuq.", "ru": "Сегодня холодно.", "tr": "Bugün hava soğuk." } },
      { "en": "It is raining.", "native": { "uz": "Yomg'ir yog'yapti.", "ru": "Идёт дождь.", "tr": "Yağmur yağıyor." } },
      { "en": "What is the weather like?", "native": { "uz": "Ob-havo qanday?", "ru": "Какая погода?", "tr": "Hava nasıl?" } }
    ]
  },
